    "created_at": "2024-08-06T21:58:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-06T21:58:34Z",
    "body": "An (somewhat underwhelming) alternative would also be keeping the `.decode()` spec as is, and documenting that `HTMLImageElement` insertion is not a \"relevant mutation\" unless inside a `<picture>` element, but that still creates edge cases where we reject but we don't want to do so, like:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nimg.srcset = \"foo.png\";\r\nimg.decode(); // I think ideally we want this to resolve.\r\nemptyPicture.appendChild(img); // The effective source doesn't change here, but it's a relevant mutation so we reject the decode() promise.\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
